{"objects":[{"id":"flow","instance":"instance--b96dad5f-c519-5a1f-a718-912ca4a86c02","objects":["attack-action--1","attack-action--2","attack-action--3","attack-action--4","attack-action--5","attack-action--6","attack-action--7","attack-action--8","attack-action--9","attack-action--10","attack-action--11","attack-action--12","attack-action--13","attack-action--14","attack-action--15","attack-action--16","attack-action--17","attack-action--18","attack-action--19","attack-action--20","attack-action--21","attack-action--22","attack-action--23","attack-action--24","attack-action--25","attack-action--26","attack-action--27","attack-action--28","attack-action--29","attack-action--30","attack-action--31","attack-action--32","attack-action--33","attack-condition--1","attack-condition--2","attack-operator--1","attack-operator--2","attack-operator--3","instance--8b844ad4-4067-5f7a-a2a8-e2f0f33dd8cd","instance--a00341c1-9627-5cc9-8a33-05cba8504150","tool--mimikatz-1","instance--106e77fe-747a-5a1e-89dc-6db607b3e38e","instance--44c63c83-a0c7-5ddc-a350-57216c2924ac","instance--3536a568-610f-5570-bba9-6dfe97bc9c2e","instance--ed6039fe-678b-5ae9-9576-73e6ea35b0c8","instance--7e8c9301-c3f8-55e9-8894-e81f1b6203d9","instance--3d75b4ae-3541-5ff2-b4f5-0d67b8bb9252","instance--56b40d44-cc57-5e8b-b320-779a685089fd","instance--3bb881aa-a5ab-51ba-b53d-89d26964ce7d","instance--2f7dea11-1cac-5e37-a118-e523d554ebf7","instance--cf28f86b-f872-50eb-b161-5e2afe841328","instance--3e0f78a3-bb54-55bd-8490-3453d5e06d04","instance--a37796a0-93b2-51bb-be4b-2a9a9e7e35e1","instance--f9e616ac-2310-573d-8995-336b82cf51af","instance--77414a6f-10f0-5dbb-b428-351706ad11fd","instance--48a9b359-fe45-5ce4-ad44-4a9a39004014","instance--92ee8792-942a-5a8c-9c2e-9bc59b33f65a","instance--d10e3bf2-a50f-5852-a99e-152c31cdbbe9","instance--3345d394-31f5-5c1e-ad3f-b0146f944331","instance--59f73335-26d3-506f-bca1-bad3ce4ad928","instance--5cd14511-0567-54e9-a615-81261d2dcc77","instance--cff34f89-682d-528d-920c-6b2d4ac309b2","instance--69f384b3-dc5a-5dbe-abae-1e12e04cd093","instance--29e3e490-4488-5aaf-9882-1c2b9617223c","instance--eb09c011-e0af-5bc8-ac75-3929ced4a65a","instance--aaed1ef6-6978-5a66-983b-51be56c74b70","instance--d190f90c-4784-50da-ad09-085edc636fbd","instance--aea2bdc0-1966-536f-8fcb-83ba0a637462","instance--d6e18896-02c8-5f5d-9dd0-a5c3d1330815","instance--f0a36fe4-f78c-51ab-b7fc-0b9451066ca7","instance--8aad72e9-6796-5400-a4d9-43700df3ca9b","instance--d5fec3a6-8e72-50ff-99ff-1859b400aadd","instance--79b60279-21e6-5f56-8fe0-fecad4b17188","instance--cc6770e2-6da0-5bd1-98d3-f392c71f3007","instance--1e9627bb-5d3b-564d-a878-4f81b693700b","instance--ee45461e-6650-59d0-a994-006c35dacfc9"],"properties":[["name","Exchange servers under siege from at least 10 APT groups"],["description","ESET Research has found LuckyMouse, Tick, Winnti Group, and Calypso, among others, are likely using the recent Microsoft Exchange vulnerabilities to compromise email servers all around the world"],["scope","threat-actor"],["author",[["name","ESET Research"]]],["external_references",[["item-1",[["source_name","www.welivesecurity.com"],["url","https://www.welivesecurity.com/2021/03/10/exchange-servers-under-siege-10-apt-groups/"]]]]]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--ad592d05-6969-5b51-98a8-1ad9b6aab896","120":"instance--5850a8f4-8241-5e73-9bf0-dcd376cd5025","150":"instance--0da1498f-3beb-5916-a249-e0410a4a81e4","180":"instance--d3632784-7391-5a29-83e2-edab51db56c6","210":"instance--8bc47ca5-ca73-5a04-a9ea-918608f10871","240":"instance--6546eef6-c5ad-516e-a417-89916e651648","270":"instance--244e5a69-f465-564e-9d2c-93d4da44fc57","30":"instance--6a1fca3c-fdb6-536a-bbea-61ac2349a700","300":"instance--043a5b44-2864-5565-abce-1909204e5485","330":"instance--e10eb918-2b0b-56f4-9c82-f345ce21276c","60":"instance--33a99d1b-dad8-51f6-be74-e1614db9151b","90":"instance--380c79e9-b1eb-547c-bf01-a011db1201c1"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--1","properties":[["name","Tick deploys first-stage webshell"],["description","On 2021-02-28, Tick (also known as Bronze Butler) compromised the webserver of a company based in East Asia that provides IT services. This means that the group likely had access to the exploit prior to the patch\u2019s release \u2013 in this case at least two days before.\n\nThe attacker used the following name for the first-stage webshell:"],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0003","technique":"T1505.003"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--4f4d03a8-4502-5010-997b-9943e254395b","120":"instance--cefe62ac-5b6e-5ead-84fc-b4c632913a73","150":"instance--4d07a740-2467-5b95-ac8d-4a2ee8edd11e","180":"instance--1205f03c-a457-5a0b-87ef-3bbb7aac110f","210":"instance--96e7dc6a-9f86-5f69-8d45-a566303cd4c0","240":"instance--66237af6-bb19-5a51-9fa2-cbc4a96186f5","270":"instance--836dfd42-b475-50ca-9acf-4f11bd32b89f","30":"instance--efe92997-cc5c-538a-90bc-c09ffb1379f4","300":"instance--9c4a24ae-1426-5cb5-9d7c-792e6dd325b7","330":"instance--06c6a74a-ca7d-5703-88ea-a06a0933d21a","60":"instance--5e4f84e5-56b7-5b8f-9bc3-b4d59d371123","90":"instance--019deb6a-bab3-57db-9a53-11e3564bf7a4"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--2","properties":[["name","Tick deploys Delphi backdoor"],["description","We then observed a Delphi backdoor, highly similar to used by the group. C&C addresses used by this backdoor are and ."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0011","technique":"T1105"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--0ce35aea-35a2-52ae-a67b-985306bdefe7","120":"instance--312639d5-e6d9-57b1-850d-28f0a1eac2f6","150":"instance--9551a25e-2558-512e-9894-dd64a8d662bf","180":"instance--403becce-e0ad-5dcd-bc14-7c00453907da","210":"instance--2305f501-2712-5ec6-9d4e-1371b011e937","240":"instance--cf1b8cf6-1cbd-5afb-b653-aa693889dab5","270":"instance--1d3dc59a-40a0-5670-aa3e-1304ff762003","30":"instance--77063d4f-503a-5e9b-b622-15aa2cc6a8e7","300":"instance--beaab67f-8a54-5982-8c5d-9d2ed2d42c9f","330":"instance--4d3274ff-ef14-5a53-99be-01575194a98e","60":"instance--4154a6bf-290b-5fce-a557-5dc0f3e700fb","90":"instance--2992bc0b-df57-54e5-a17b-03a964338c09"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--3","properties":[["name","LuckyMouse drops and installs webshell"],["description","LuckyMouse operators started by dropping the in , then installed a variant of the webshell and issued a GET request to using ."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0003","technique":"T1505.003"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--0f6e4da7-a5f4-54d7-866f-3bc6e8bcb019","120":"instance--015254b5-0906-577e-b3e3-3899f837d118","150":"instance--f7af5b8c-330a-58d5-b0da-a3d5f0bc6ad0","180":"instance--9f27ab21-2382-567d-b022-74ad5a29bd08","210":"instance--d799eb0a-7600-5b1a-a298-c47a78ceae4b","240":"instance--911c2c52-5974-5e08-b0b6-a9084d57c6ee","270":"instance--286444b4-97a1-58cd-9ca3-cffa04a15351","30":"instance--92192c38-5143-50e0-8c39-a96ea86e32e2","300":"instance--82bb3de0-bea5-5651-a1de-583283258c6d","330":"instance--4f0945c8-f644-50ce-8796-fea52a29dda1","60":"instance--16c43a2d-7356-521d-a507-5922e2c3337b","90":"instance--abce5c62-339a-5ed5-a0b8-dd66136cfe2f"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--4","properties":[["name","LuckyMouse issues GET request"],["description","LuckyMouse operators started by dropping the in , then installed a variant of the webshell and issued a GET request to using ."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0011","technique":"T1071.001"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--a469636c-0cb2-50b9-92f9-644c8aa98197","120":"instance--d57b3a21-e910-5879-8148-40165cea451a","150":"instance--58250ef4-5bb4-5bf3-b33e-89493bbb395d","180":"instance--3e769cf2-c1e5-5d2e-81d4-892f48ce4d86","210":"instance--f6499e41-749c-5d7f-9346-96c08d0d5dfd","240":"instance--d9dcdfc8-5f42-546a-803a-0efcd5d4cf91","270":"instance--c9afd0f6-97ce-57b2-9d60-3557b6214809","30":"instance--75f82155-f5ff-5619-8bf8-aae22937cab0","300":"instance--25e2d26e-1b35-56bd-b9aa-096c2d3b0e3c","330":"instance--e0483688-da10-5376-8cf2-050bcc3b70f0","60":"instance--1293d9cc-16b2-5c67-a453-bd144aab133a","90":"instance--2b43cd52-10db-5b15-8ad5-c4b59496528b"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--5","properties":[["name","LuckyMouse attempts to install Soldier backdoor"],["description","Finally, they attempted to install their (aka Soldier) modular backdoor that uses the aforementioned IP address as its C&C server."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0011","technique":"T1105"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--54fc1f38-f4e3-523e-b07c-73889b0d8df7","120":"instance--9cf45948-7040-5d7a-a1d5-3cb4db0c1af6","150":"instance--13bb13cc-e02b-51d2-8d7d-40e5613b6e5a","180":"instance--e33bc6ee-771e-54fe-a772-74dfdaad420d","210":"instance--286f51a3-8fc6-55ec-978e-8b05ebda3655","240":"instance--14659696-be77-5460-beb1-4b5eac126e43","270":"instance--f48ed1a6-2895-5cd2-9b1c-e30ac2bc8921","30":"instance--7b803e61-16ac-5720-92cd-8f2a456a52b7","300":"instance--76c24361-5143-5c43-8e4d-707c619e6038","330":"instance--f395cfc7-395a-5001-9552-a4fec6dbc53a","60":"instance--760885bb-9294-5a5b-93a2-a410e1ea4112","90":"instance--8e0d1a12-8611-598d-9a7d-40f2525e4781"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--6","properties":[["name","Calypso deploys first-stage webshells"],["description","On 2021-03-01, compromised the email servers of governmental entities in the Middle East and in South America, which means the group likely had access to the exploit as a zero day, like LuckyMouse and Tick. In the following days, Calypso operators targeted additional servers of governmental entities and private companies in Africa, Asia and Europe using the exploit.\n\nThe attacker used the following names for the first-stage webshell:"],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0003","technique":"T1505.003"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--7cccbcd0-a724-54fb-be4f-ac523d26f7d0","120":"instance--738e44b2-1357-5eb3-82bd-8a0ce8942b72","150":"instance--d31f4735-6339-5929-8d7c-d30863cf166f","180":"instance--2252393d-d801-5931-ad38-4b53374a9880","210":"instance--065b5ad5-023a-5336-b458-e9c9dcda2976","240":"instance--5ea0dd2b-5eac-51f8-855a-4cbcb801bc2d","270":"instance--bba66874-a069-56c6-bb95-967cb3cefc9e","30":"instance--6377c09d-ecb4-5567-a2f4-4dde56ff4f98","300":"instance--ede3430f-b16b-58ae-be71-1d1f1a194336","330":"instance--7772f482-8ee2-569a-b600-7528c065d4e0","60":"instance--98139a98-16b0-54fe-8c77-3473c1b520cd","90":"instance--5cb9cc95-e190-5a68-985d-0a94d39299e6"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--7","properties":[["name","Calypso loads backdoors via DLL hijacking"],["description","As part of these attacks, two different backdoors were observed: a variant of PlugX specific to the group (Win32/Korplug.ED) and a custom backdoor that we detect as Win32/Agent.UFX (known as Whitebird in a ). These tools are loaded using DLL search-order hijacking against legitimate executables (also dropped by the attackers):"],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0004","technique":"T1574.001"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--5150f7cc-6f25-5eb3-a6fc-5099ced4caf4","120":"instance--64a408ce-c543-55d6-a9dd-206ce7cadbb2","150":"instance--1b71e413-cfd2-528c-8792-dc7dd1bb9938","180":"instance--aa12ce11-0165-52b6-b72d-e4d9070e9fbb","210":"instance--5d8b0f08-14bc-58f4-9316-b25a92dd09a6","240":"instance--34f96b84-9453-53f2-ae07-d28c04665e6c","270":"instance--415f1d54-1cd4-5ba7-8071-4aa99bc946ac","30":"instance--18834cac-b4c4-57b0-88ea-5a62fdb27cf9","300":"instance--de4f9957-1ac6-5782-86ea-f1a3b6a9ad13","330":"instance--8eff940b-86bb-556f-8c85-c7c47577b3ed","60":"instance--14a123fd-5626-5e69-8257-6dcd64c28ec0","90":"instance--02294ff1-7261-5db8-8e0d-b9e818922053"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--8","properties":[["name","Calypso uses Mimikat_ssp"],["description","Finally, we also observed a variant of a tool known as Mimikat_ssp that is available on ."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0003","technique":"T1547.005"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--180f2983-9c1a-56f4-99d6-c990125f7baa","120":"instance--c7f65318-7600-57f4-a8ac-992357e695ff","150":"instance--95523e1a-0a1d-52ef-944c-23f9cbc50233","180":"instance--bc8eb48d-411d-5877-aa9b-966476b71207","210":"instance--4cc5026e-07f9-5327-9912-5d278a0a3321","240":"instance--d6a7d51d-39a4-5eb3-8831-f23437781b95","270":"instance--cac30e05-5f01-5b4f-b5c0-6b975297df2d","30":"instance--cb0751b0-c027-5895-a460-a72e48920c71","300":"instance--f41cdc1f-abb7-5ff7-81c2-bf2235a7faab","330":"instance--b114cbda-9ec8-5612-b2f8-93c36811cafb","60":"instance--f28e5296-2041-5fe9-992d-4c70d549191e","90":"instance--3ea39244-da0f-5435-8745-f2afa8b13872"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--9","properties":[["name","Websiic deploys first-stage loader and config"],["description","This cluster was identified by the presence of a loader as its first stage, generally named or , and an encrypted configuration file, generally named ."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0011","technique":"T1105"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--db5fab04-54d4-5eec-a429-185861eb2719","120":"instance--985391bd-d017-5935-ab31-3b4b56331b02","150":"instance--092bb98d-fc30-5f69-b6b7-e3024f3ec65a","180":"instance--755129e6-612e-5b63-a780-1c886d98909b","210":"instance--431723d9-dd8c-5190-9dab-6f346173c044","240":"instance--5b9fb821-54fe-5f22-bba3-038263245910","270":"instance--3c6777cb-6430-544b-b31a-01b198524553","30":"instance--c070071b-a9a3-52fe-8956-a51744db200b","300":"instance--a9a4289c-d995-5783-9544-a8b45052eb56","330":"instance--344009cc-e024-5c68-9246-51e85e00d45c","60":"instance--86c77621-2c1d-59c3-b398-e62f4b48a3dd","90":"instance--67627b08-1913-5f3d-8318-52d3bda9c1c3"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--10","properties":[["name","Websiic modifies service registry and restarts service"],["description","The loader stops a specific service identified in the config and creates a new entry under the Windows service registry (the service\u2019s filename is provided by the config). It sets two keys and . The first one contains the path to a DLL while the latter contains the export to call ( in this case). Finally, it restarts the service that was stopped at the outset."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0003","technique":"T1543.003"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--6b7baffd-afaf-5472-9af2-a263119a77ef","120":"instance--83f38e63-e29a-53f4-99d9-927a195c453f","150":"instance--3e720145-b7a1-5bd6-8a7d-bb13519675d1","180":"instance--bdce060f-d96c-5b06-b8f4-1ab1527fd01d","210":"instance--a4feb251-e6e3-5680-a712-d59c92f73ccf","240":"instance--9a564ca6-b753-5b06-880c-b3aac25c1e73","270":"instance--76861a89-f006-5e0d-8c5b-ebdcb5e926dc","30":"instance--cf41e64d-4a4b-58d9-9962-72d278b2c489","300":"instance--ac1d6edd-482f-5f13-9348-b605afcc260c","330":"instance--ed78dfa1-f300-564f-b2cd-6c99552b9a68","60":"instance--979accb3-1b3e-5af4-9182-78392cbaf904","90":"instance--ae721c42-320e-5ea4-9c77-339a05b6e12f"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--11","properties":[["name","Websiic loads second-stage DLL"],["description","While the loader was deployed on all victims from this cluster, the second stage (also a loader) was observed on the computer of only one of the victims and was located in . The DLL has an export namedthat contains the main logic and uses the same XOR encryption loop as well as the same technique to dynamically resolve the Windows API names as seen in the first stage. It loads the following DLL with an argument extracted from the registry key ."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0005","technique":"T1218"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--f1e35721-7ac2-54fe-bcf6-5456d2faeaa3","120":"instance--3ff6777e-fcba-5b31-bf0f-3ddf77f6030d","150":"instance--cc6192f9-21a5-5d1a-b954-6a52d989b82d","180":"instance--62a87260-0181-5f49-bc05-733216e4d822","210":"instance--2f2d05c5-8e60-5ac2-b7af-e03027d67957","240":"instance--79c1ec18-d792-5d3d-a7bc-d94fe8b124cf","270":"instance--a035d357-e930-5d33-ab8d-d0314092d036","30":"instance--3af551b8-f6ac-5f54-9f6d-403fecdc69eb","300":"instance--298b5d2a-bf93-51e9-b052-19ce36114a5d","330":"instance--c8ea0da0-a19a-5766-b0d1-8524844a59d1","60":"instance--a204f87d-ace7-5a9e-b3d1-13202bdc5c7b","90":"instance--fff4de11-3f84-52c8-bb77-192210612a62"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--12","properties":[["name","Winnti drops webshells"],["description","Starting 2021-03-02, a few hours before Microsoft released the patch, the Winnti Group (also known as BARIUM or APT41) compromised the email servers of an oil company and a construction equipment company both based in East Asia. This indicates that this APT group also had access to the exploit prior to the patch release.\n\nThe attackers started by dropping webshells at the following locations, depending on the victim:"],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0003","technique":"T1505.003"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--cac05670-e90e-512c-99cc-c0adf909c3ef","120":"instance--43922820-ddd3-5742-a88d-49c20f8e3fd5","150":"instance--884271a6-8d7b-5c96-9ece-61be4126898b","180":"instance--373a94ef-653d-5c24-96f7-d0cf326d3aea","210":"instance--e58b782a-e75e-5141-bdf0-6d47dbed96bd","240":"instance--5960e46a-3307-5101-b96f-f1bae10e323d","270":"instance--a5ae1125-6ca5-54f1-b9d3-0091a0a38367","30":"instance--e7c521dd-fe09-528b-bb67-1ec53389b876","300":"instance--582e0864-cb5c-5de1-b6c0-e162ae91e8bc","330":"instance--3d5550f3-3e33-5d71-b71e-db2a0a957e5e","60":"instance--b83fc757-0bd4-5b63-a13e-e5b8ef5956d2","90":"instance--2a745819-837b-5585-a366-81a34117a6e5"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--13","properties":[["name","Winnti deploys PlugX RAT"],["description","At one of the compromised victims we observed a PlugX RAT sample (also known as Korplug) with C&C domain and . Note that was with ShadowPad and the Winnti malware. On the same machine, during the same timeframe, we also observed some malware, not yet fully analyzed, using as its C&C address but at the time of writing we don\u2019t know whether this is related to the Exchange compromise or not."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0011","technique":"T1105"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--2accaaf8-d071-542e-9a10-06866a96b394","120":"instance--75ef5b2f-7c71-566e-baf2-29f54ced8138","150":"instance--73017f0a-a5f3-5dca-b91c-a2d37bcfe21b","180":"instance--2f1b6e5f-d3b0-59e5-b3c8-6c1399d1ce2a","210":"instance--c7aedd91-3346-5b75-9e3a-842851881a25","240":"instance--2146989b-d8a2-53f0-8a1c-cd3d976227e9","270":"instance--1b0bbd91-fa2a-5897-96d0-9e5918961c9c","30":"instance--e6b73353-364e-5586-a07b-e1fdc92ad2d3","300":"instance--0fdc5473-d5b9-5fed-91a3-21958da6287b","330":"instance--fd1cd9e0-5761-5725-801f-bf88b65914e8","60":"instance--a58b8357-6abc-58d7-ad2b-bec48fffcd9b","90":"instance--e8daf33f-0240-5544-9f99-3be7ac96fc1d"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--14","properties":[["name","Winnti decrypts payload and executes loader command"],["description","At the second victim, we observed a loader that is highly similar to previous Winnti v4 malware loaders such as that mentioned in our white paper on . Like that Winnti v4 loader, this loader is used to decrypt an encrypted payload from disk and execute it using the following command:\n\nwhere is the decryption key used to decrypt the payload stored in ."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0002","technique":"T1059"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--c80ca3ef-db0a-5372-968e-c17eb31a79ca","120":"instance--69989f45-927f-57be-92e5-5102fccd9f11","150":"instance--9b02c549-b183-5406-a100-249fb1868d16","180":"instance--c1d2a890-ed8d-5123-92d5-ceeaa937ee87","210":"instance--b785b7b9-02d5-5d04-be0c-0d02d4f85620","240":"instance--cde2d3fb-a23f-5188-9d7d-6c7f3cd3cebb","270":"instance--3fa59d94-25bb-5c51-af21-1a7c1fd91f66","30":"instance--fdd04191-1a03-5134-b88e-a55240471931","300":"instance--dddeb587-c160-5bdc-a385-f5d294f11e92","330":"instance--a13b6b46-2b8e-5660-b86f-03747a07fe24","60":"instance--d996db22-4d65-536a-83bf-a1db02b37136","90":"instance--258e2cac-1806-5147-8d61-a10d64a86e46"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--15","properties":[["name","Winnti drops malicious DLL implant"],["description","Once executed, this loader drops a malicious DLL at the following location:"],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0011","technique":"T1105"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--878d252f-de04-5857-ad0a-e8560794a9aa","120":"instance--bf65c103-2305-50be-8098-7718a8b010c5","150":"instance--348f71b8-78ee-5edf-accb-cd536c0db67d","180":"instance--e786d536-88e4-5ad4-8526-ae120c505f45","210":"instance--d3f3806c-3238-5b69-a0ca-334a1453e3dd","240":"instance--6dc42515-8e0a-5d8f-9dcb-cc6f0eb80f24","270":"instance--6a335c70-0c01-578c-9e01-614ace562750","30":"instance--c34e4c14-a710-535c-afd4-17d8ea759e88","300":"instance--60b19ce6-d4d3-5ce5-b2fe-3427fd0ea9a4","330":"instance--dea41a44-5c5a-520f-8975-25088fdd166c","60":"instance--e8f2f47b-1824-589b-af23-ab4291258936","90":"instance--67989025-38e3-56c8-b903-f474fc067511"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--16","properties":[["name","Winnti uses Mimikatz and password dumpers"],["description","Additionally, we observed various Mimikatz and password dumping tools."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0006","technique":"T1003"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--dbfe6415-cd2c-55f2-9509-06b6668ef23a","120":"instance--79ca45e2-afd7-51fa-9574-5085c7de4c84","150":"instance--39171cfe-3bf6-5200-b6f5-e97e3b047db7","180":"instance--8cda146b-7259-56b2-b337-56038a1f52d3","210":"instance--a662f8bf-2723-58c0-a1a8-9af9497cf428","240":"instance--a9b75b15-3be0-5e64-8132-40b87e7ae405","270":"instance--31896ecd-322b-5a41-bd1e-0b7a30b9d9d1","30":"instance--60868276-2726-597d-8f57-8aa7fc9c0738","300":"instance--4f5668fa-b6ef-57cc-93da-5cd1e1727a22","330":"instance--b022a562-9020-587c-a5be-97d254cc8f11","60":"instance--cf452b0f-192e-5357-ba8c-fbae1a6e4ae0","90":"instance--012cc6fc-0a37-5e6e-b9b7-07f3bcd2d02c"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--17","properties":[["name","Tonto Team deploys first-stage webshell"],["description","On 2021-03-03, Tonto Team (also known as CactusPete) compromised the email servers of a procurement company and of a consulting company specialized in software development and cybersecurity, both based in Eastern Europe.\n\nIn that case, the attacker used for the first-stage webshell."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0003","technique":"T1505.003"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--a73f63ad-1c10-59c2-82aa-bef4ae8f64e0","120":"instance--62757838-a58e-5d41-b7e3-1ccc64e8cdbf","150":"instance--3462202b-a91d-5325-abfe-876a63049484","180":"instance--72959cd4-5e05-5d69-a145-8b6f35720646","210":"instance--d3b85082-8de6-5ffd-8abe-c9e1ec43f533","240":"instance--0a22ffab-8bbc-55b1-85ec-df74e4a120f6","270":"instance--548b3ba1-955f-5e04-b6e8-064cc259e7a6","30":"instance--6f0a37c5-db81-5459-92c1-bc8ab8cd1fd3","300":"instance--e81be898-f7c2-56a0-a705-d2aba8831f75","330":"instance--8f207ed6-cb63-551c-9a40-583fac14fe80","60":"instance--8b44546f-f8e4-5d12-b172-99f9507395eb","90":"instance--f61db455-1665-504d-85b4-5fd5d40fbcc2"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--18","properties":[["name","Tonto Team downloads payloads with PowerShell"],["description","The attacker then used PowerShell to download their payloads from ."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0002","technique":"T1059.001"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--223a73a7-07a6-5688-bc70-e7fbf2c8afd4","120":"instance--2184e59f-b6bd-5ca7-8254-3872e152a964","150":"instance--eed82efc-7573-5ccf-97d8-e3f88a2337bb","180":"instance--453ded0c-8246-59f2-a14f-beca9e751cd6","210":"instance--143e4619-312d-5cbc-acc5-efed5f6c0164","240":"instance--659cf4a8-ca80-5204-8b8d-3240f6f370da","270":"instance--2dac3e32-a8df-582e-845a-3a7b1d510c1d","30":"instance--6ab42faa-5ba5-5c44-b387-40b1d021e500","300":"instance--96e5ad82-e4af-5995-8b69-6df7d7ce2490","330":"instance--a960fdd4-4889-5426-a406-4761d11be5ab","60":"instance--42df375f-d3e2-5d47-9faa-324aecbbf064","90":"instance--51395417-94d2-5b5a-881c-7b6cc63ade4e"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--19","properties":[["name","Tonto Team loads ShadowPad via DLL hijacking"],["description","Those payloads consist of a legitimate and signed Microsoft executable used as a DLL search-order hijacking host and a malicious DLL loaded by that executable. The malicious DLL is a ShadowPad loader. The C&C address being used by ShadowPad here is and the communication protocol is HTTPS.\n\nIn addition to ShadowPad, the attacker also made use of a variant of the Bisonal RAT highly similar to a Bisonal variant that was previously used during"],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0005","technique":"T1574.001"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--25dacfeb-3a3d-51fc-91b7-64ee405fe041","120":"instance--5a984174-ce49-510d-b6b6-d4f0e0ee332f","150":"instance--f2167f56-1cf9-5fea-a726-d003a591d391","180":"instance--70c47af3-1817-5ae2-9f6e-38421d85f808","210":"instance--cfd506cd-f673-5f4f-a5ff-5854ad8a39d5","240":"instance--b78e4cb3-2b2b-5706-8d59-d252dd134505","270":"instance--73410cfd-8533-5545-94b7-c06859fcd4a8","30":"instance--760fe684-ea1e-52a0-87e8-fa0bc5d62d70","300":"instance--fa30f213-64f3-55b5-85cd-9dbf46e0e8dc","330":"instance--0dbe5c9b-c2db-5139-a300-8054f3a8e205","60":"instance--a78137f8-a78e-563e-ad44-749594629166","90":"instance--626b6c26-479d-5895-a619-ee3dbb14136d"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--20","properties":[["name","Unattributed operators deploy webshells"],["description","Starting 2021-03-03, we observed the compromise of email servers at a software development company based in East Asia and a real estate company based in the Middle East where ShadowPad was dropped by the attacker and that we were not able to conclusively attribute to any known groups at the time of writing.\n\nThe attackers used and as first-stage webshells and dropped ShadowPad at the following locations:"],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0003","technique":"T1505.003"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--93ee4f51-8321-58fb-b05f-3a6fd3a6a8ab","120":"instance--02ee2d77-fc8c-55cc-8958-e3d0b5ead581","150":"instance--15aaf9f3-3996-5f9b-bee4-47f2963a0df4","180":"instance--1ae13e0a-be4e-5658-ba6d-c941c0d5cafb","210":"instance--87590098-5adb-5af7-aa75-039447d58b2b","240":"instance--87dee187-bf66-5b52-81e0-15b789ab6a7c","270":"instance--25c474c1-a795-5124-95ce-3e6163b067d2","30":"instance--ae371f09-8eae-53a7-a14c-34f9e72904fd","300":"instance--9ecc9c80-603d-5760-b2b6-f850dfd3eddf","330":"instance--b9543d3c-a7f9-50a6-b8a1-3fd4c6dddd56","60":"instance--cba1b44c-d7c9-5ebb-8433-b63b0b91427c","90":"instance--1c5f2ea2-c075-51ba-9f13-69b716c352cf"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--21","properties":[["name","Unattributed operators drop ShadowPad"],["description","The attackers used and as first-stage webshells and dropped ShadowPad at the following locations:"],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0011","technique":"T1105"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--da12a10e-e9d8-58e0-9dda-e871f0fcaf7c","120":"instance--6e98f91f-940c-5b7d-8e4e-950f2c88b044","150":"instance--02b3e90f-a9f8-5908-b936-c779b2c570d8","180":"instance--5c256240-99ff-5907-aca7-0f81639a7419","210":"instance--e42c995a-6770-583f-9a60-afcdf41d5501","240":"instance--eee0e52c-22be-5b9b-819e-097b65b643d8","270":"instance--d4973194-aaba-5ce5-99ba-7d7c8bca7b50","30":"instance--91b449e9-d343-56d1-9376-8a2655b8032b","300":"instance--23579e20-df5a-5dad-9088-26b612c3c5aa","330":"instance--2ed64056-576c-519d-b8c7-4e1f2c06b6e9","60":"instance--c59d1168-f011-5687-803d-27aa797d72e2","90":"instance--321449b3-3e1e-5b4b-aab6-507e5ad1c36c"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--22","properties":[["name","Unattributed ShadowPad communicates over HTTPS or DNS"],["description","One of the ShadowPad samples uses as its C&C address using the HTTPS protocol while the second sample uses using the DNS protocol, which is less common."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0011","technique":"T1071"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--9f68185c-8d0f-5e34-b869-da9c17407e5d","120":"instance--99f65057-0748-5b22-b7a8-859b8cb9d46c","150":"instance--1c6c577b-3682-579f-9d80-c1a4c9632dd5","180":"instance--0372a821-a640-58c2-a8f9-f391b8fb0045","210":"instance--bd12903c-f92d-5416-a20f-eedd38d108f9","240":"instance--a221d4df-2c16-5e25-a121-f7cfbb303fb7","270":"instance--550d9be5-209a-50fa-99b8-4dfe7669b693","30":"instance--042db59c-d5d0-5002-ac74-85e947cc6579","300":"instance--2ce3cd55-fc34-5aac-8112-e6cc8fcd707a","330":"instance--55903f51-17c6-554e-8180-6f2511efa2b6","60":"instance--2b4af278-cf58-556d-9fa5-254ca76fcb98","90":"instance--a84c2c43-a2a5-5904-906d-da6a186887bd"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--23","properties":[["name","Opera cluster deploys webshell"],["description","From 2021-03-03 to 2021-03-05, ESET telemetry shows this activity targeting around 650 servers, mostly in the US, Germany, the UK and other European countries. Interestingly, this threat actor was consistent in the naming and location of their first-stage webshell, always using ."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0003","technique":"T1505.003"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--08881caf-1468-53e2-baa3-c9da43e73b47","120":"instance--5344d679-b2e1-5528-bed5-6fe3fbc90036","150":"instance--f1a3ca80-d761-5917-981a-9d35e6a5161e","180":"instance--bb22e51a-29ce-531e-b80e-4a1d5343b453","210":"instance--380340c8-8f15-5075-a390-ac1b2706e43f","240":"instance--b8ca794c-8bea-5f4c-a746-ad3b31fd2d36","270":"instance--fb5c8b1f-7cc5-58a3-a457-0edfdefa168c","30":"instance--a124cc0a-728c-5b30-8b8b-2171584014e7","300":"instance--7d09cfe0-ac57-5093-a7ce-7c31042d3449","330":"instance--829e634f-5069-5370-8381-e0687a22b00e","60":"instance--0fbffc26-a516-5fcd-9fff-e9aee12c6467","90":"instance--96917b9c-4649-5345-82ac-b4e793881bfe"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--24","properties":[["name","Opera cluster downloads Cobalt Strike components and loads via DLL hijacking"],["description","Then on a few selected machines, they executed a PowerShell script, shown in Figure 4, to download additional components from . The final payload is Cobalt Strike, which uses the same IP address for its C&C server. Cobalt Strike is loaded via DLL search-order hijacking against a legitimate Opera executable named (SHA-1: ) using a DLL named (SHA-1: ) that decrypts and loads a shellcode from (SHA-1: ).  We noticed that was also used to distribute malicious files."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0005","technique":"T1574.001"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--6e9515e3-2497-5444-80ce-9466679d2504","120":"instance--25d30ffe-4a4f-53ec-a34d-de6cc58a2fb0","150":"instance--43abd457-ad7e-5db6-b146-d159a2936c52","180":"instance--f22410a7-1bbd-5943-9121-cf9edb5a0991","210":"instance--4a2a2f86-5543-5514-866c-4d5f4f5bcb3b","240":"instance--f2011b06-5138-5056-a1f2-0a96e9738966","270":"instance--a9d1b1c1-44f0-5281-b6b0-9133e0a433dd","30":"instance--c9339355-ad0b-5e98-9f42-ef0c11d380dd","300":"instance--dec744bc-b6ae-5258-bcb1-83f01a7bb747","330":"instance--54f63fd7-f831-5401-a04f-600f5e780c31","60":"instance--1dd30294-3434-540a-8b5f-d8bc1e3de794","90":"instance--e414165a-d829-5c22-ab74-6aa5e50c83d3"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--25","properties":[["name","Operators install IIS backdoors via webshells"],["description","Starting 2021-03-03, we observed that on four email servers located in Asia and South America, webshells were used to install so-called IIS backdoors."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0003","technique":"T1505.004"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--ce3f20b8-daf0-5682-a74a-dd9eb1251abb","120":"instance--08418575-7199-5323-8082-8e1d88a1ec11","150":"instance--15627176-59a5-5797-816e-a6cab3ea9da9","180":"instance--242a8d77-274b-5d18-ba35-771f6e0de836","210":"instance--d01bb126-419a-5d3b-a9cf-7b8df1d59112","240":"instance--0b76a14d-f362-5d5a-995f-2e318539789f","270":"instance--d534a23c-ea17-5a19-96f9-740e77b559a2","30":"instance--9b134899-2cf4-5fcd-9412-5363985ac68c","300":"instance--1bb6a59f-c750-5aca-a7c7-cecaf9c9f1f7","330":"instance--a346b253-e85b-53ff-8e33-33aaa8c928da","60":"instance--0c9baf75-2ba0-51ff-b084-c1044ff899fa","90":"instance--b86b5b84-3a18-51f2-b888-17161b8c5d47"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--26","properties":[["nam